      "writtenOn": "2024-04-16T17:57:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For where the value comes from, see the comment I sneaked in right before yours above.\n\nThe `VkFormatFeatureFlags` returned by `VkAndroidHardwareBufferFormatPropertiesANDROID` are ONLY relevant and representative of actual format capabilities when we are using an *external* format\n(https://registry.khronos.org/vulkan/specs/1.3-extensions/man/html/VkAndroidHardwareBufferFormatPropertiesANDROID.html#_description). That being said, as for whether we could use the same sampler if it has different format features...\n\n[info ripped from link above] \nAndroid hardware buffers with the *same* external format must have the same support for:\nVK_FORMAT_FEATURE_SAMPLED_IMAGE_FILTER_LINEAR_BIT, VK_FORMAT_FEATURE_MIDPOINT_CHROMA_SAMPLES_BIT, VK_FORMAT_FEATURE_COSITED_CHROMA_SAMPLES_BIT, VK_FORMAT_FEATURE_SAMPLED_IMAGE_YCBCR_CONVERSION_LINEAR_FILTER_BIT, VK_FORMAT_FEATURE_SAMPLED_IMAGE_YCBCR_CONVERSION_SEPARATE_RECONSTRUCTION_FILTER_BIT, and VK_FORMAT_FEATURE_SAMPLED_IMAGE_YCBCR_CONVERSION_CHROMA_RECONSTRUCTION_EXPLICIT_FORCEABLE_BIT. \n\n\"Other format features may differ between Android hardware buffers that have the same external format. This allows applications to use the same VkSamplerYcbcrConversion object (and samplers and pipelines created from them) for any Android hardware buffers that have the same external format.\"\n\nSo with that, I think we are good to not check this equality here. Removed! Marking as resolved",
