      "writtenOn": "2024-04-16T17:57:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Theoretically I suppose it *is* possible that the `uint64 external format value` could \u003d\u003d `(a known uint32 format value with a 0 value uint32 appended)`, so we certainly can add a bit to nonFormatInfo to determine that. It fits with no issues. Done!\n\nNote:\nI\u0027m still simply checking if `info.fFormat \u003d\u003d VK_FORMAT_UNDEFINED` here rather than calling `nonFormatInfoAsUInt32()` first and checking the first bit because I imagine we want format info earliest in the key for fastest possible determination if two conversions are the same, so this sequentially makes more sense and is clearer IMO.\n\nI *could* add a small method of `usesExternalFormat()` to `VulkanYcbcrConversionInfo` if we want to have that logic be in one central place, but the logic that determines that should never really change. So personally, this feels comfortable to me as-is.",
